From 09e03ab59480f459691be93453305435a4d48a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:54:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/47] Frame generation motion, 2D texel box, menu strip mode,
 parallax, minimise fix

- Frame generation: each 3D draw writes its own motion (second render target, previous
  frame's constants re-run through the vertex program), so FSR 3 no longer smears
  characters and moving objects with the camera's motion.
- Texture coordinates: only programs that pass coordinates on as given get wrap read as
  clamp (TexcoordsAsGiven), fixing the rampart sky's smeared, hard-edged strips.
- Frame capture from a menu (g_capture_asked, captures\ beside the game).
- Extension::TexelBox / PixelKey::texbox: a 2D quad's stage 0 reads stay half a texel
  inside its coordinates, so upscaled glyphs no longer pick up the sheet's next picture.
- Parallax on material surfaces (g_surface_depth): the view ray marched through the
  occlusion map as depth; the picture and its maps read at the moved coordinates.
- ResizeSwap keeps the swap chain's size while the window is minimised (an abort under
  frame generation as the window was hidden).

