From d02db318efa43b0aaa92a902ff26760d43365574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:16:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/47] Full-width widescreen targets, FSR anti-aliasing before
 the UI

- Targets are wider by the screen's shape over 4:3 in widescreen (aspect_), so 100%
  renders as many pixels across as the screen shows; scale conversions per axis
  (ScaledRect, copies, slope bias, box filter, rtshift through TexInfo::aspect).
- AntiAlias (framegen.h) / FsrAa: AMD FSR's upscaler at the frame's own size. The
  frame's 3D takes a Halton sub-pixel offset (Extension::Jitter, motion.zw, after the
  motion is taken); at UiStart (or at present) motion and depth are drawn at the
  frame's size, FSR runs, its output is copied back and the draw's state set again.
- Frame generation gets the jitter; the per-draw motion target is kept for either.
- ffx_upscale.h from FidelityFX SDK v2.3.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
