From 86fdbbf9fede3d27472b913c91468c90b7c1991f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:42:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/47] FSR and DLSS upscaling of the frame's 3D, DLSS
 anti-aliasing

Upscaling (g_upscale): from the frame's first draw into the back buffer
until its UI starts, the 3D is drawn into the top left part of the
target (the scene) at the anti-aliasing's size for the quality, then
made up to the whole target by AMD FSR or NVIDIA DLSS before the UI.
Viewports, scissors, partial clears, copies, polygon offset slopes,
point sizes, the render-target shift and parallax's view follow the
scene; anything that reads the frame early closes it first. The scene's
depth and motion are made whole after, for later 3D and frame
generation. A 2D screen's frames, and the first 3D frame after one,
draw whole.

Streamline is shared by DLSS frame generation and DLSS (loaded at the
start for either), with DLSS on its own viewport. DLSS-G's depth is
declared reversed, as it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
