From 5816483743c3d121086fe497d40530e6c2162920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:47:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/47] Reactive mask, texture bias, ambient occlusion;
 constants edited off the upload heap

- Upscaling's texture bias by preset: Quality as sharp as the output size, Balanced half, Performance
  none (the HD pack's reads were most of the 3D's cost on a shared-memory GPU)
- A reactive mask for FSR and DLSS from the frame's blended effects that write no depth
- Ambient occlusion (low, high) from the 3D's depth before the anti-aliasing gathers it
- FSR sharpening amount from the settings
- The draw's vertex constants edited in ordinary memory and uploaded once: the extension and the
  motion's copy read the write-combined upload heap back, 12 ms a frame on a Ryzen Z2 Extreme
- Parallax's march reads at one level of detail, without anisotropic taps or the bias
- XBE_PERF: GPU time by part of the frame, a draw's steps on the render thread, barriers and
  pipeline changes; XBE_AA_MIPBIAS and XBE_AA_REACTIVE to weigh the costs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
