From cf0d0e529944e192812f4b2762181fa1dacd4ae4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:32:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/47] Depth convention from the view: ambient occlusion, FSR
 and DLSS read near at 0

The renderer turns the title's depth round, and this title's own has the near plane at its top, so the
buffer and its copies hold the near plane at 0 (FrameView's near_w at 0, far_w at 1). Ambient occlusion
read it as near at 1, which put every pixel at the near plane and gave no shade at all; FSR's upscaler
and the Streamline constants (DLSS, DLSS frame generation) were told it was inverted too. Now all take
it from the view. Ambient occlusion's radius set for the title's units (a few millimetres): 200 low,
250 high. XBE_AO_VIEW, XBE_AO_RADIUS and XBE_AO_STRENGTH to look at and tune it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
---
