From c666237234004033205a5c52f754579611d473a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:30:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/47] DLSS frame generation: Reflex's limit at twice the
 game's rate; controllers for ImGui through SDL

The NVIDIA app's DLSS override turns DLSS-G into dynamic multi frame generation aimed at the display's refresh (138
under G-SYNC at 144 Hz): it made 2 to 3 frames for each of the game's and held the game at 46 to 55 a second, so it
played in slow motion. Reflex's frame limit, which with frame generation is on the frames shown, set to twice the
game's cap (120 for 60) keeps the game at 60 and one frame made for each; measured on an RTX 5080 with the override
on: 60.0 game, 120.0 shown. The dynamic target frame rate is set too, and a log line says when frames shown run
past twice the game's while it is held below its cap.

input::Raw reads a controller without the game's hook; the renderer feeds the first one to ImGui's navigation
(D-pad, sticks, A, B) each frame, so a PlayStation or Switch pad drives a game's menu, not only XInput's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
