From c32067df5bfe9a7881f941b76efdf7cfcc102e8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:18:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/47] Ray traced bounce lighting, smoothed by full-size
 guides; the passes share one pipeline maker

Bounce lighting (gpu::kRtLighting, rt_gi.hlsl): at half the 3D's size (XBE_RT_GI_SCALE), each pixel finds its
surface in the scene and sends 2 rays (XBE_RT_GI_RAYS) over its hemisphere, up to 2500 units (XBE_RT_GI_REACH);
each hit takes on that draw's picture times its vertices' colour (the game's light), and their mean, times the
strength (4 at 100%: this title's colours are dark), is the light arriving: the courtyard's water lights the carved
wall above it. rt_giapply.hlsl smooths it across a 5x5 of the bounce target's texels on the same surface (depth and
normal weights), multiplies it by the surface's albedo at the full size, so a picture's detail stays sharp in it, and
adds it into the frame before the anti-aliasing. About 0.3 ms at 1080p on an RTX 5080.

Guides (rt_guide.hlsl, drawn once a frame when a pass needs them): each pixel's albedo (RGBA8, alpha 0 where the
scene is not what the frame drew) and its octahedral normal (the face's, bent by the material's normal map),
roughness and metal (RGB10A2), at the frame target's size: the smoothing's, and what a denoiser takes.

rt::Scene::Trace draws any pass (ambient occlusion, reflections, bounce, its smoothing, the guides) with a pipeline
made the first time a pass and target format are asked for; up to two targets.

