From 02f1da857ebfbc5ebc455c46d6bd554880b1ed81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:05:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/47] The bounce lighting's own denoiser, for cards whose
 anti-aliasing does not denoise

When no vendor's denoiser takes the frame (AMD FSR; DLSS without Ray Reconstruction's
files), the bounce target is gathered over the frames (rt_gitemporal.hlsl): reprojected by
the frame's motion, its history taken only from texels that held the same surface (as deep
as the camera's move says, within 5%, facing the same way), each frame weighted 1/n up to
24, a spark held to four deviations above what the surface gathered. Then smoothed by an
edge-aware a-trous wavelet (rt_giatrous.hlsl, 4 passes of 5 x 5 taps 1, 2, 4 and 8 texels
apart) guided by the moments' variance, large where few frames are gathered. About 0.2 ms
at 1080p on an RTX 5080. XBE_RT_DENOISE 0 never, 2 always; XBE_RT_DN_FRAMES, _PASSES,
_SIGMA, _DEPTH, _NORMAL, _SMOOTH_DEPTH, _SMOOTH_NORMAL; XBE_RT_VIEW 10 shows the frames
gathered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
