From 6c6bbd2392908bddc4414b2eb307140c3134d068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:20:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/47] The port's own denoiser takes the reflections and
 ambient occlusion too

When no vendor's denoiser takes the frame, ray traced ambient occlusion is gathered over the
frames before its blur and multiply (rt_aotemporal.hlsl: up to XBE_RT_DN_AO_FRAMES, 16), and
the reflections are drawn into a target of their own (ReflectionsAlone), gathered
(rt_refltemporal.hlsl: a few frames for a mirror, up to XBE_RT_DN_REFL_FRAMES, 12, for the
roughest that reflects) and smoothed twice as widely as their roughness blurs them
(rt_reflatrous.hlsl, the second pass drawn over the frame). Both take history only from the
same surface and hold it within what this frame's neighbours span, so a contact shadow or a
sliding reflection does not trail. The guides keep each pixel's surface (world normal, view
depth) a frame for this, as a fifth target. About 0.35 ms more at 1080p on an RTX 5080.
XBE_RT_VIEW 11 the reflections alone denoised, 12 the frames they gathered; 11 for ambient
occlusion its frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
