From f298962a91bea475831791482cdaf1e0da4e9774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:59:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/47] Ray tracing: brightness-neutral lighting, water,
 lights, shadows, sky, shafts, quality

- Bounce lighting takes the place of the game's flat fill: the room's average
  bounce (rt_gimean.hlsl, eased over about a second) is subtracted, what falls
  short of it takes out a share of the frame's own light, so rooms keep the
  brightness the game gave them; g_rt_lighting_strength scales it.
- Reflections conserve energy (alpha = w * max F) on every material.
- Water (Extension::Water): drawn with the frame's 3D it is a smooth, rippled
  mirror with water's Fresnel in the reflections pass; drawn after the frame is
  anti-aliased it is captured late (Scene::LateCapture), copied into the next
  frame's scene as an instance of its own (mask 2) moved by the camera's move,
  its picture's alpha saying where it is (rt_water.hlsl).
- Lights: additive glows, flames and spells sampled by the bounce lighting
  (RIS over up to 32, a shadow ray); flat sprites (Extension::ScreenLight) put
  back where they show by the frame's depth; their light kept out of the
  room's average.
- Characters (Extension::Character) in an instance of their own (mask 4):
  soft shadows from a tilted light above in the ambient occlusion pass, and
  their metal shines by its colour (CharacterGloss).
- Sky light: the frame's sky colour and share (rt_gimean mode 3) brought by
  bounce rays that leave the scene upward.
- Light shafts (rt_shafts.hlsl): in-scattered sky and lights, marched at a
  quarter size, gathered over frames, added over the frame.
- g_rt_quality (low, medium, high): rays, sizes, reaches and steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
