From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:49:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/47] Ray tracing: steady lights, no sky haze in the light
 shafts

- The lights sampled are the same every frame, up to 128 (the scene's own
  first, then those drawn flat); the turn through 32 a frame flickered.
- A light drawn flat is put at the depth at its triangle's middle (the same
  place sample to sample), a third as bright as the scene's own
  (XBE_RT_LIGHTS_FLAT), its light softened near it; at most 0.75 a sample.
- More candidates a light sample is picked from (4, 6, 8 by quality).
- The bounce lighting goes through the port's own denoiser with DLSS Ray
  Reconstruction too (XBE_RT_GI_DENOISE=0: not).
- The light shafts leave the sky's light out (XBE_RT_SHAFTS_SKY 0): outdoors
  it laid a haze over every open place, 1.4 times the frame's brightness,
  which the doors' radial blur took to white in HDR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
