Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:23:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/47] Ray tracing: light shafts steady and subtle (the
 flicker in rooms past the courtyard)

The shafts were what sparkled: lights drawn flat (a fountain's spray, motes, a
glow's sprite) lit the air of whole rooms with a grainy haze, and the gather
held its history within the 3 x 3's least and most of a sparse, noisy march,
so it threw the gathered light away each frame. Now only lights drawn in 3D
light the air (Scene::EmissiveSolid), the march is smoothed over its 3 x 3 and
the history held within the 5 x 5's mean and spread, and the shafts are laid
over as a screen lays light, a glow of about 0.15 at most (a fountain's water
and a ghost's body, drawn added, are large lights that washed rooms out).

