Subject: [PATCH 20/47] Ray tracing: only steady glows are lights, none bigger
 than a torch's flame; a gain on the lit side

A sword's swing, a hit's sparks and a spell's burst were lights for the few
frames they lasted, grain on the walls the denoiser had no time to settle:
a glow's picture now has to be drawn as a glow 20 frames in a row
(XBE_RT_LIGHTS_STEADY) before it lights anything. And no light counts more
area than a torch's flame (XBE_RT_LIGHTS_AREA, 4000), in the bounce
lighting and the light shafts: the save room marker under Hector, mist,
beams of light and ghosts' bodies lit whole rooms their colour.
XBE_RT_GI_BOOST (1) scales the light added above the room's average, the
lit side of the contrast as XBE_RT_GI_FILL is the dark side; its default
is still being tuned.

