Subject: [PATCH 23/47] Ray tracing: realism fixes (untested): see-through
 leaves and ivy, characters lit as the room, steady room light

- Blended pictures with clear parts (ivy, fallen leaves) are cut-outs to rays (XBE_RT_CUTOUT_BLEND 16), so the
  stone behind them is no longer shaded in black boxes
- Characters give up their own share of the game's light as the bounce falls short (XBE_RT_GI_CHAR_FILL 0.6)
- Characters throw no bounce light (Hector's red sash lit the floor red): bounce rays meet the world alone
- The room's average bounce is held over the frames since the cut (XBE_RT_GI_HOLD 1200), not eased toward the
  view's, so turning the camera no longer changes the room's light
- The guides take the latest of draws laid on one face (a save door's ironwork over its moving glow)
- Neutral defaults: fill 0.3, boost 1.0, flat lights 0.8

