From b003f73b601f0801cfeaf28bc9f4fbeab71f0197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:29:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/47] Ray tracing: see-through layers to ambient occlusion;
 the water's glow gathered by bounce rays

- Every picture's alpha is looked at as it is uploaded (AlphaKind), the game's own as well as a pack's: one with
  clear parts is a cut-out when drawn blended, one faint all over (glass, a haze, a sheet the game fades) is no
  surface to rays at all
- Ambient occlusion on a blended cut-out darkens its pixel as much as the cut-out covers it (a lamp's pale panes and
  a clump of leaves' edges were shaded as dark as stone); the floor under a faint sheet is not shaded black
- Only the first 16 draws of a picture a frame are listed as lights (XBE_RT_LIGHTS_PER_PICTURE): the save room's
  water glows in some 500 draws of one picture, which filled the list of 128 before the candles got in. All of them
  still light the room: the bounce rays gather the glows they pass through (XBE_RT_GLOW_BOUNCE 1), outside the
  room's average
- XBE_RT_CUTOUT_LOG: how rays take each picture drawn blended

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
