Subject: [PATCH 30/47] Ray tracing: the bounce lighting as a gain on the
 game's own light; the frame's draw by its depth

The bounce lighting's lit side was added in the surface's picture's colour: the save room door's panel, a bright
cyan picture the game draws dark by its vertices' colour, lit as bright as its picture. It is now a gain on the
frame's own light, colour by colour (frame x (colour + alpha): BounceApply blends DEST_COLOR, SRC_ALPHA), the share
the fill takes out as a surface gets less than the room's average given as it gets more (twice its own at most), so
what the game drew dark stays its colour. The debug views draw in the frame's place (BounceApplyView). TopDraw takes
the scene's hit nearest the frame's depth within 2%, the latest of those at one distance.

