From 18c37434ee9619de9f0174bf65999e3fe435df90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:00:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 32/47] Ray tracing: lights' samples kept frame to frame, glows
 remembered off screen, flames drawn flat as lights

The bounce pass keeps each texel's light sample (rt_gi.hlsl's second target) and
resamples it with the next frame's candidates (ReSTIR's reuse over time,
XBE_RT_LIGHTS_REUSE 4). rt_glowmem.hlsl keeps the glows seen in slots moved with
the camera, sampled while off screen (XBE_RT_GLOW_MEMORY 20 s).

A glow is steady by the title's texture data, not the renderer's copy: torches and
candles animate by palette and were never lights. Sprites drawn off the screen give
no light. The bounce light's gain leaves the frame's effects (the reactive mask) as
drawn. XBE_RT_LIGHTS_LOG logs blended draws and the lights listed; XBE_AA_TRACE
where the 3D closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
