The pipeline library (cache/shaders/pipelines.bin) now has a list beside it (pipelines.list): every pipeline the
game makes or loads, with its shaders' and root signature's bytes and which compiled shader each shader source's key
is. At start, the listed pipelines the library lacks are made on background threads, and the listed compiled shaders
the shader cache lacks are put in it, so no room's first frame compiles a shader or makes a pipeline. A release can
ship its own list beside the exe. --prepare-shaders does the same on the card the game will use and exits, writing
its progress (prepare.txt) and a stamp of the card, driver and release list (pipelines.stamp) for a launcher to
compare. kernel::g_file_read lets a game change a file's bytes as they are read.

