Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:17:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 39/47] Ray tracing: glows in an instance of their own, the
 lights' light with an end, the sky's light held

- The world's glows (emissive draws) go into a bottom level and instance of their own (mask 8), which only the
  rays that gather glows (GlowsAlong, LightAlong) cross. Every other ray crossed them as candidates passed over one
  by one: the save room 5.27's 500 water glows stacked on its walls slowed the frame past 1/60 s, the game with it.
- A light's light eases to nothing toward XBE_RT_LIGHTS_REACH (2500 view units, the bounce rays' reach; the list's
  fourth column): a purple lamp in view lit the mountains across the valley behind it.
- The sky's light is held over the frames since the cut (rt_gimean.hlsl 4): its share of the frame rises toward the
  most seen (XBE_RT_SKY_RISE, 60 frames) and does not fall, its colour eases (XBE_RT_SKY_EASE, 120). Measured from
  each frame alone, the outdoors grew brighter as the camera tilted up and darker as it tilted down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
