From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:51:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/47] The F10 menu's frame capture also keeps the screen as
 shown (screen.bmp)

A capture kept the console's 640x480 frame (final.bmp), before widescreen, ray tracing and upscaling: what the player
saw could not be told from it. The back buffer is now read too, before the port's own menus go over it, and written
at the output's size; HDR (scRGB or HDR10) is brought to SDR, the scene's white to white, the highlights eased in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
