From 40b26ba8727686c7c1156b79c71261a6aa78a9af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:08:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 45/47] Ray traced lighting that relights the room; DLSS's
 out-of-memory warning no longer taken as a failure

Lighting looked little different from ambient occlusion alone: the game's flat fill stayed most of each room's
light (XBE_RT_GI_FILL 0.3), and a surface was raised at most 70%. Now the fill gives up to 70% (0.7) as a surface gets
less than the room's average, a lit one is raised up to three times its own (XBE_RT_GI_LIFT_MOST 2, knee 0.8, boost
1.5), and the scene's lights are brighter (XBE_RT_LIGHTS_GAIN 40): torches and lamps light pools on their walls and
floors, and the light falls off into the dark. The Lighting strength setting at 50% gives about the old look.
The bounce lighting fades out by 10000 (XBE_RT_GI_FADE, was 20000), and its gain fades with it, set against the
room's average as unfaded: the sky cards past 5.9's rampart took a green and orange smear of the rampart's light.

Streamline's eWarnOutOfVRAM (39) is a warning with the work done; taken as a failure, it sent Ray Reconstruction to
DLSS anti-aliasing, that to none, and the 3D to the output's whole size (4K from 2227x1253) for good. Now said once
and taken as done. The graphics card's memory against its budget is logged (MemoryCheck): its budget at the start,
when it goes over and back, and every 30 s with XBE_PERF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2YaGgWez1ZqKbAmtKk
---
