From 05f169956bb7eea911dd5769c19a165dbc2ce343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:54:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] Slowdowns, enemy after-images and a leak: texture pack
 pictures let go, ray tracing within a budget

The texture pack's pictures (BGRA8, with their normal and ORM maps) were kept for every guest texture slot that ever
showed one, about a quarter of a GB a room, never let go: a long session filled a 16 GB card and Windows paged the
rest, the slowdown that grew the longer one played. TrimReplacements now lets go of those not drawn from in 60 s
(XBE_TEX_IDLE), and under pressure (past 0.8 of the budget, XBE_TEX_PRESSURE) those idle 5 s or more, oldest first,
down to 0.7; one drawn again is asked for again. MemoryCheck reports the card's memory by kind every 2 minutes (every
10 s with XBE_PERF) and when it goes over; XBE_MEM_TRACE=<frames> a line a check.

Ray Reconstruction was made again at each room change when frame generation was off (the first 3D frame after a 2D
screen is drawn whole), and without Streamline's swap chain its garbage collection never ran: 2-3 GB a room. Frames
drawn at another size for a while (60) no longer remake it, and Streamline's factory is used whenever DLSS runs.

Ray tracing's cost is held to a budget (XBE_RT_BUDGET, else 36% of the frame at the cap: 6 ms at 60): the bounce
lighting's rays halved once (4 to 2) while ray tracing's GPU time is over it, back once there is room, 90 frames
between changes. The save room's water glow, gathered by every bounce ray, went from 6.6 to 4.1 ms.

Characters drawn into a picture of their own with the frame's depth (an enemy's spawn and attacks, its after-image)
closed the scene early: the characters after them were drawn after the ray tracing ran, unlit, and not anti-aliased.
Such a picture now gets a depth of its own (AfterDepth), the scene's depth copied and stretched into it, so the scene
stays open and the after-images are still hidden behind what is in front of them.

GPU timestamps for the ray tracing's passes (XBE_PERF's line); EndDrawCapture's inputs for every draw with
XBE_CAPTURE_ALL; the early close's reason logged (LOGR_FIRST).

