From ac201d503a3d81d57b8e7bcf7233acecd19d6710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:34:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ray tracing: the Path traced quality

A quality above High (g_rt_quality 3, RtPathTraced; the passes' quality stays High's): the bounce lighting as a path
tracer's (rt_gi.hlsl's PathTraced). One path a pixel at 0.71 of the frame's size (XBE_RT_PT_SCALE, XBE_RT_PT_PATHS),
each followed two bounces: the ray from the surface meets a first vertex, whose light is the lights' there (a light's
point picked of XBE_RT_PT_TRIES candidates, a shadow ray toward it) and what a second ray from it brings, the sky where
it leaves the room or the second vertex's picture times the lights' light there and the game's own light there
(XBE_RT_PT_END of it, 3: the artists' light stands for every bounce after the path's end). The first vertex's own game
light is not taken (it arrives through the second), so what nothing reaches is dark.

rt_giapply.hlsl applies it outright (gz.w): of the game's own light only an artists' share is kept whatever the rays
say (1 - XBE_RT_PT_FILL 0.65 x the Lighting strength: 0.35 at 100%), the rest set against the room's average by
brightness (raised against the average or XBE_RT_GI_MEAN_FLOOR, the more, up to XBE_RT_PT_MOST 3 times, eased from
XBE_RT_PT_KNEE 2), the light's hue against the average's on what is raised alone (on the whole, a night courtyard was
tinted purple wherever its brazier's light was most of the little there was; colour by colour against the average,
a channel the room had little of was raised without end). A character keeps the room's share and is never raised.
The denoiser's smoothing a pass more at the frame's size (6, the last 32 texels apart).

At 4K DLSS Balanced on an RTX 5080: the ray tracing 4.7 ms a frame against High's 3.5 (at the frame's full size 7.1,
the look the same); 5.3 in the Mountains against 4.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2XTW6h6BAjQxxWwA47
