From ce681a62c1a364311023cbbcc2bfa76dc744aeef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:42:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ray traced lighting: the lights' candidates picked per tile,
 the remembered glows capped, the carried state kept finite

The lights' sample (rt_lights.hlsli's PickLightKept) picks which light each candidate is on for a tile of 8 x 8 pixels
rather than per pixel (the point on it still per pixel, and each pixel's choice kept frame to frame as before): the lanes
of a wave read one light's vertices and picture rather than 32 lights', and the Abandoned Castle's save room (94 lights
listed, 800 glow sprites over its water) goes from 11.4 ms a frame of lighting at 4K DLSS Balanced to 6.2, the frame
from 19.5 ms to 13.5 (XBE_RT_LIGHTS_TILE=1: as before). The glows remembered off screen capped at the 12 brightest
(XBE_RT_LIGHTS_REMEMBERED; rt_glowmem.hlsl's row 4 ranks them); the list read from the glow summary's new row 3 as a
texture (LightInfo) rather than the constants; ambient occlusion's glows along a ray at 4.

The bounce lighting's carried state kept finite: rt_gi.hlsl's output and kept point, rt_gitemporal.hlsl's history,
rt_gimean.hlsl's levels and hold, rt_giapply.hlsl's taps and average, and RoomBounce reads the room's average back each
frame (ReadMean, a ring without a wait) and starts the lighting over (rt_restart_) when it is not a number, which the
eased hold would otherwise keep for good with the lighting off until the ray tracing was turned off and on. XBE_PERF's
lines: the room's average, the scene as last built (g_rt_scene), XBE_RT_LIGHTS_SHADOW=0 to time the shadow rays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2XTW6h6BAjQxxWwA47
