From 3100e6cfa70105a55e2c98f149df29e1dbc99932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:03:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ray traced lighting: the glows' sprites thinned in the scene,
 the Path traced quality's candidates fewer

The scene holds XBE_RT_GLOWS_PER_PICTURE (48) draws of a glow's picture at most a frame: the listed, then every
stride-th of the rest, each standing for stride of them in the bounce rays' gather of the glows they pass (GlowsAlong's
weight, Look::rough_bias for a glow): the save room's 800 water sprites overlapped over its pools and a ray through them
visited most of their acceleration structure (its lighting 5.6 ms at 4K DLSS Balanced to 4.1, the frame 13 to 11.4).
The lights' candidates at Path traced 4 for the pixel's light (High's 8) and XBE_RT_PT_TRIES 2 at a path's vertices
(4): each pixel keeps its choice frame to frame, and the extra ones cost 0.3 ms for no less flicker. XBE_RT_GLOW_BUDGET
(12), the glows taken along a ray at most, a knob.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2XTW6h6BAjQxxWwA47
