From 0e00e0e7dbfd66d61d0b50fe314e64e13adede7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:48:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ray traced lighting: the sky held through a room's change,
 the room's average through a camera cut

The sky's hold (SkyLight, rt_gimean.hlsl 4) is kept through a room's change and starts over only at the lighting's
restart: measured afresh in each room, the bridge before the courtyard had no sky in view looking along it (its planks
dark) until the camera tilted up past the sky cards, then bright looking down too. While none is in view its share
falls by 1 / XBE_RT_SKY_FALL (3600) a frame, so a hall entered from the open air loses it in a minute. The room's
average starts over when the view was lost (rt_room_reset_), not at a camera cut within the room. XBE_RT_SKY_DEPTH
(0: off) counts the frame's pixels that deep and deeper as the sky too; XBE_RT_LIGHTS_TILE the tile's size; the sky
held on XBE_PERF's line (ReadMean's second ring). (Tried and left: the average held a minute, the sky from 12000
units out at 0.3: the night courtyard 5.9 went brighter and lost its brazier's purple to a blue floor.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2XTW6h6BAjQxxWwA47
