From 2f046e2e5c62e209ec102d1cf3ab612dd03a0120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PlatinumMimic <julianharmon100@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:29:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ray traced lighting: HDR's highlight rise by a pixel's
 surroundings; a picture's glows listed by where they are

In HDR the rise above the knee went by each pixel's own brightest channel, and with a peak of 8 over scene white the
curve's slope is 36 at white: the ray traced lighting's grain on a lit wall, a level's change in one pixel, was a
flicker of a third of 4000 nits as the camera turned. Now the rise goes by the brightest channel over nine taps two
pixels apart, so the grain keeps the share of the light it has in SDR.

Which of a picture's many draws are listed as lights and kept in the scene goes by where each is (GlowPlace: the
first vertex's position, to 32 units), not by the frame's draw order, which the title changes as the camera turns
(the save room's 800 water sprites). XBE_RT_GLOWS_BY_ORDER=1 keeps the old way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P39J2XTW6h6BAjQxxWwA47
---
